\f1\fs22 The Resonance Cluster occupied a different sub-level to the K-LAB, connected to it by a corridor that smelled of carpet adhesive and recycled air. An underground rail line ran from here to somewhere beneath Ruined Castle, which Chip had been told about but not yet seen. He didn\'92t want to see it. He didn\'92t want to see most things.\
Johnny walked three paces ahead of everyone, which he seemed to believe was a leadership technique. The three Sages trailed behind him in their florid suits, looking like a delegation of retired circus ringmasters who\'92d wandered into a hospital. Kleo, Solo and Chilo. Chip had memorised their names the way he memorised fire exits.\
Chip kept to the back. His new Shakti Enterprises lab coat had too many pockets and not enough structural integrity for a man of his dimensions. He adjusted his security badge for the fourth time, then stopped adjusting it because the repetition was making him feel like a suspect.\
\'93As you can see, gentlemen,\'94 Johnny announced, sweeping a hand toward a holographic display the way a car salesman sweeps toward a vehicle he hasn\'92t read the spec sheet for, \'93we\'92ve made significant progress in decoding the Gyges Disc\'92s properties.\'94\
Dr Ortolan stood beside the display with the expression of a man whose presentation had just been hijacked by someone who couldn\'92t spell \'93resonance.\'94 The display showed concentric circles pulsing and shifting, their edges blurring and reforming. Chip had seen patterns like these once, in a classified Fridge Force incident briefing. Three senior agents had suffered seizures from viewing similar recordings. One of them still couldn\'92t eat soup without assistance.\
\'93If you\'92ll observe these readings,\'94 Johnny continued, which was unnecessary, because everyone was already observing the readings, on account of them being the only thing in the room that moved.\
\'93And you believe these are messages?\'94 Solo asked, stepping closer to the display than anyone with a working survival instinct would normally allow.\
\'93Not believe. Know.\'94 Johnny corrected a two-thousand-six-hundred-year-old man with the satisfaction of someone who\'92d been waiting all morning to correct somebody. \'93Dr Ortolan has confirmed that each pattern corresponds to universes with different universal gravitational constants.\'94\
Dr Ortolan opened his mouth, presumably to clarify what he had and hadn\'92t confirmed, but Johnny had already moved on.\
\'93What about time?\'94 Solo said. \'93Gravity shifts. Surely time shifts too.\'94\
Dr Ortolan frowned. \'93Temporal variance?\'94\
\'93That\'92s extremely dangerous,\'94 Chip said. He hadn\'92t meant to say it. Everyone looked at him. \'93I mean. Fridge Force has. That is.\'94 He tried to organise his thoughts into a sentence that wouldn\'92t get him arrested. \'93Stasis technology operates on similar principles, and temporal calibration has been known to cause. Incidents.\'94\
\'93Nonsense,\'94 Johnny said.\
Everyone stared at him.\
\'93What kind of incidents?\'94 Johnny added, recalibrating.\
\'93Classified.\'94\
There was a silence that Chip found uncomfortable and Johnny found theatrical.\
\'93A mere suggestion,\'94 Chilo said, sliding into the gap as though he\'92d been waiting for it to open. Which, Chip suspected, he had. \'93If gravity differs between universes, surely time flows differently as well. Perhaps a matrix calibration accounting for relative chronological displacement might\'97\'94 He stopped, waved his hand. \'93But I\'92m no physicist.\'94\
This was the sort of statement that sounded modest until you thought about it for more than two seconds. Chip thought about it for three.\
\'93And what did Fridge Force regulations say about such calibrations, young Chip?\'94 Kleo inquired, with the gentle weight of someone who already knew the answer, had known the answer before the question existed, and was asking primarily to hear how you\'92d handle the telling.\
Chip looked between his new employers and the spectre of his old ones. \'93The Food Preservation Secrets Act prohibits me from discussing specific technical details, but\'97\'94 He dropped his voice, because whispering felt less treasonous than talking. \'93There\'92s a reason stasis fields are locally contained and never allowed to resonate with one another.\'94\
Dr Ortolan\'92s frown had deepened past confusion into the territory of a man performing rapid calculations he didn\'92t like the results of. \'93It\'92s an interesting thought,\'94 he admitted. \'93We could modify the phase variance compensator to include a temporal coefficient. With appropriate safety measures.\'94\
\'93Precisely what I was about to suggest,\'94 Johnny said. \'93Let\'92s implement that immediately.\'94\
\'93I strongly advise against this.\'94 Chip could feel the colour leaving his face and suspected it was heading for the exit. \'93At minimum, we should conduct a full containment assessment before\'97\'94\
\'93Mr Stockwell,\'94 Johnny interrupted, \'93your expertise in fresh food is noted, but this is cutting-edge physics. Dr Ortolan, proceed with the modifications.\'94\
Dr Ortolan looked at Chip. Chip looked at Dr Ortolan. Neither of them proceeded.\
Then Dr Ortolan turned to his workstation, because Johnny signed the purchase orders.\
Solo drew close to Chilo while the lab technicians began reconfiguring equipment according to instructions Johnny was relaying from Dr Ortolan\'92s notes as though he\'92d composed them himself.\
\'93What are you doing?\'94 Solo whispered.\
\'93Accelerating inevitability,\'94 Chilo replied, his voice barely audible.\
\'93This isn\'92t what we discussed,\'94 Solo hissed.\
Chilo merely smiled.\
Chip stood very still. He knew about temporal resonance events. He knew what happened when stasis fields stopped being locally contained. He knew these things because he\'92d read the classified reports, and he knew he\'92d read the classified reports because he wasn\'92t supposed to have read them. Telling anyone would solve one problem and create seven others, all of which involved prison.\
He turned, quietly, and walked toward his office. He needed to compose a message to Sarah Jacobson. Before these people turned the Resonance Cluster into a crater.
